<article class="env-definition" id="03J4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03J4">Definition <span data-tag="03J4">29.58.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say the integer $n$ <em>bounds the degrees of the fibres of $f$</em> if for all $y \in Y$ the fibre $X_ y$ is a finite scheme over $\kappa (y)$ whose degree over $\kappa (y)$ is $\leq n$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say the <em>fibres of $f$ are universally bounded</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000663754" id="a0000663754-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if there exists an integer $n$ which bounds the degrees of the fibres of $f$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>